# Embedded Cubeless Codex Ops

This directory is the embedded operating root for `UnrealMCP5_6_1`, the Cubeless Unreal MCP repository targeting Unreal Engine 5.6.1.

## Bootstrap

From the repository root, read in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `codex/AGENTS.md`
3. `codex/projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`

Do not use the external `../CubelessOps` repository as the active authority for this repository unless the user explicitly asks to compare or synchronize operating docs.

Parent workspace agent files such as `D:\Git\AGENTS.md` are also not part of the active 5.6 MCP operating model. This folder carries its own agent, workflow, policy, and project binding rules.

Sibling repositories and Git submodules are not required for routine work in this folder. The sample project and UnrealMCP plugin under `MCPGameProject/` are handled as part of this repository.

## Active Facts

- Repository: `UnrealMCP5_6_1`
- Remote: `https://github.com/cubeless2-lgtm/UnrealMCP5_6_1.git`
- Engine: Unreal Engine 5.6.1 at `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6`
- Verification target: Win64 Editor
- Android packaging: out of scope unless the user explicitly re-enables it
- Embedded project binding: `projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`

## Directory Map

- `agents/`: role boundaries for planning, MCP implementation, upstream sync, release verification, and Unreal C++ review.
- `docs/policies/`: Git, approval, path, memory, permission, and cost rules.
- `docs/workflows/`: repeatable procedures for bootstrap, orchestration, MCP updates, Unreal work, and reviews.
- `projects/`: project bindings. `UnrealMCP5_6_1.md` is the active binding for this repository.
- `scripts/`: local maintenance helpers.
- `skills/`: repo-owned skill packages copied from shared Ops for reference or future installation.
- `snapshots/`: historical instruction snapshots.

## Synchronization

This embedded copy was derived from `D:\Git\CubelessOps`. Changes made here stay local to `UnrealMCP5_6_1` unless the user explicitly asks to mirror them back to the external shared Ops repository.
